<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Diego de Almagro the Younger</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1520–1542</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Diego de Almagro II</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/diego-de-almagro">Diego de Almagro</a> the Younger was the son of the conquistador Diego de Almagro and an Indigenous woman of Panama. Leading his father's followers, he had <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francisco-pizarro">Francisco Pizarro</a> killed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lima">Lima</a> in June 1541 and proclaimed himself governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peru">Peru</a>. The royal governor Cristóbal Vaca de Castro defeated him at Chupas in 1542, and he was executed at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cusco">Cusco</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/diego-de-almagro-the-younger.jpg" alt="Diego de Almagro the Younger" width="320" height="464" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Pueblos Originarios · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:POMA412.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
